# Force LF line endings for files that must run on Linux.
#
# A shell script checked out with CRLF fails on Linux with a confusing
# "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M: No such file or directory". These are edited on
# Windows but executed on the ABCI-Q cluster, so pin them to LF regardless of
# the local core.autocrlf setting.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.def       text eol=lf
*.py        text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
